WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.440
- I also heard you're
a talented cartoonist.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.534
So, you love doing, how do you,

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.626
how do you decide what you're gonna do?

00:00:05.626 --> 00:00:09.170
- I do cartoons, it's catharsis, you know.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.480
I've been through a lot of crazy feelings

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.440
in the last few years.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.880
So I've been doing that.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.550
And I let it take me
where it wants to take me.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:18.713
And I do painting, and I do cartoons.

00:00:19.926 --> 00:00:20.894
- That's so cool.

00:00:20.894 --> 00:00:22.346
(audience claps)

00:00:22.346 --> 00:00:23.179
- Yeah I love it.

00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:24.170
- I've tried painting, I'm not good.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.770
- Yeah, it's so cathartic.
it's so wonderful,

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.380
and a year later it tells you
what you wanted it to say.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.213
- [Kelly] Like crazy.

00:00:30.213 --> 00:00:31.080
- [Jim] Okay so this,

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.220
this is the story of
the prodigal son to me.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.660
That's my father

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.290
and that is basically
every day of my life.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.000
When I take the shell
off (audience laughs)

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.604
and I'm born again every morning.

00:00:40.604 --> 00:00:41.437
- Oh my god!

00:00:41.437 --> 00:00:43.727
- Yeah, so I did that one
on Easter and I just said,

00:00:43.727 --> 00:00:45.750
"Hey, let's shake off all this, you know,

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.310
vitriol and whatever it is

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.690
and become united again, and let's -

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.987
- That's such a healthy thing though,

00:00:50.987 --> 00:00:52.090
like using that as your vehicle.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:54.383
- Yeah, but the prodigal son one,

00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:55.979
I don't know if you can put that back up,

00:00:55.979 --> 00:00:59.040
it's quite weird-
- [Kelly] Dark?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.104
- No, it's not dark actually.

00:01:00.104 --> 00:01:00.937
- [Kelly] No, not at all!

00:01:00.937 --> 00:01:03.550
- [Jim] It looks dark and yet
what it represents from me

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:05.720
is a lot of people don't
think about these stories,

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.110
you know, the prodigal son,

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.640
the two siblings that, you know,

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.748
one goes off and gallops,
gallivants around,

00:01:12.748 --> 00:01:14.441
and the other one stays in the kingdom

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.260
and keeps it running, right,

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.460
until the prodigal son comes back.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:21.290
Well, the prodigal son is your mind,

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.900
at any one moment

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.820
you're either in your body
or you're not in your body,

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:29.371
and your mind is the prodigal
son or the prodigal daughter,

00:01:29.371 --> 00:01:30.380
- You're either present or not present.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.930
- It goes, the heart can't go anywhere.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:34.410
It has to run the body.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.620
It has to keep the blood pumping.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:38.130
And so it's stuck,

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.410
but the mind can go
anywhere it wants to go.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.243
- [Kelly] Which I love.

00:01:41.243 --> 00:01:42.600
- And sometimes that's fantastic,

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.502
except when it takes you over,

00:01:45.502 --> 00:01:49.790
and it prevents you from doing this.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:52.315
It prevents you from doing this.

00:01:52.315 --> 00:01:55.630
And all of the things and the
walk in the morning and stuff.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:02:00.429
So, sometimes when you're in,
can I say, "Hell on earth"?

00:02:00.429 --> 00:02:03.017
- You can, and I have been there.

00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:05.734
- Sometimes when you
are, that's time travel.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:10.130
You can never really, it's
very difficult to be unhappy,

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.570
if you're really in your body,

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.360
if you bring your brain back to your body,

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.310
and sometimes that's what pain is.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.932
Pain is your body
calling you back, saying,

00:02:17.932 --> 00:02:20.210
"I'm your heart and I miss you."

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.203
- [Kelly] Yeah, work on this!

00:02:21.203 --> 00:02:22.573
- Come back, come back.

00:02:23.546 --> 00:02:25.171
- That's so cool! (audience claps)

00:02:25.171 --> 00:02:26.650
I thought you meant
the black and white one

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.140
of your father, that's the one I,

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.240
I was like, "Looks a little dark,"

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:30.166
but it's great.

00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:30.999
- That was my dad.

00:02:30.999 --> 00:02:34.410
My dad is, that was I did from
a photograph of my father,

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.340
in his early life,

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.104
standing on a rooftop in
Toronto with his pet rat.

00:02:39.104 --> 00:02:40.639
(audience laughs)

00:02:40.639 --> 00:02:41.630
- Wow.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.233
- My dad was one of the
most incredible characters

00:02:43.233 --> 00:02:44.940
that you ever met in your life,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.080
the funniest man that
ever walked the earth,

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.050
and he makes me look
like, I don't know what.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.702
Like a Shakespearian tragedy.

00:02:52.702 --> 00:02:54.170
- No but you should know this about you,

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.620
like you have a really cool
vibe and light about you,

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:57.560
and you're so welcoming,

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.700
like I've only been on this
show for like five months,

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.720
but like a lot of times you meet people

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.850
and they all have walls up,

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.770
and they're so afraid
and they're so serious,

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:06.750
'cause they want to be taken seriously,

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.620
and it's like, it's really refreshing,

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.949
so thank you for being
such a light, it's cool.

00:03:10.949 --> 00:03:12.452
(audience cheers and claps)

